  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nA cold front accompanied by rain showers will move southeast\nacross the area late this evening through tonight. It'll be a\nshort window (generally between 22-05Z), with showers lasting\nno long er than an hour or two at any given location. Thunder is\nunlikely but can't be ruled out in the Toledo area and then\nalong the lakeshore, with a brief gust of wind mainly near the\nlakeshore.\n\nDry weather returns Friday and Saturday as high pressure build \nback in across the region. Slightly cooler, albeit still above \nnormal, with highs in the 60s Friday and Saturday behind the \ncold front. Chilly overnight lows Friday night in the 40s for \nmost and the low to mid 30s in the higher terrain of Northwest \nPennsylvania. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nAs high pressure departs to the east, isolated, light rain \nshowers may accompany a warm front Sunday night into Monday. Low\npressure and an upper-level low will build into the region \nthrough midweek, with rain shower chances increase Monday night\nonward. Above normal temperatures will remain in place, and in\nfact will be well above normal Tuesday and Wednesday.",
